.TH GZIP 1 2026-10-19 tugz
.SH NAME
gzip, gunzip, zcat \- compress or expand files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gzip
.RB [ \-cdfknqt ]
.RB [ \-1 .\|.\|. \-9 ]
.RI [ file .\|.\|.]
.br
.B gunzip
.RB [ \-cfkqt ]
.RI [ file .\|.\|.]
.br
.B zcat
.RB [ \-f ]
.RI [ file .\|.\|.]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gzip
compresses each
.I file
in place, replacing it with
.IB file .gz
and keeping its mode, owner, and times.
With no
.IR file ,
or with
.BR \- ,
it compresses standard input to standard output.
Run as
.BR gunzip ,
it decompresses, and as
.B zcat
or
.BR gzcat ,
it decompresses to standard output.
.PP
Decompression recognizes the suffixes
.BR .gz ,
.BR .z ,
.BR \-gz ,
.BR \-z ,
and
.BR _z ,
in any case, and
.B .tgz
and
.B .taz
for
.BR .tar .
Concatenated members decompress as one stream.
Trailing garbage is a warning, but zero padding is not.
.PP
Headers record no file name or time, so equal input always gives equal
output.
An output is never left partial: on failure or interruption it is
removed.
In place,
.B gzip
skips symbolic links and sticky files unless
.BR \-f ,
and special and set-ID files always.
.SH OPTIONS
Long options may be abbreviated to any unambiguous prefix.
.TP
.BR \-1 " .\|.\|. " \-9 ", " \-\-fast ", " \-\-best
Compression level, from fastest to best (default 6).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-stdout ", " \-\-to\-stdout
Write to standard output and keep input files.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-decompress ", " \-\-uncompress
Decompress.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Overwrite outputs, follow links, and allow a terminal as input or
output.
With
.BR \-dc ,
copy data that is not gzip through unchanged.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-keep
Keep input files.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-name
Neither save nor restore the name and time, which is always the case.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet ", " \-\-silent
Suppress warnings.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-test
Test the integrity of compressed files.
.TP
.B \-\-rsyncable
Accepted, without effect.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.PP
GNU gzip's
.BR \-r ,
.BR \-l ,
.BR \-v ,
.BR \-S ,
.BR \-N ,
.BR \-a ,
.BR \-L ,
and
.B \-\-synchronous
are refused, the
.B GZIP
environment variable is not read, and only gzip data is decompressed.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on error, 2 on a warning.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
gzip \-9 access.log
tar cf \- src | gzip >src.tar.gz
zcat src.tar.gz | tar xf \-
.fi
.SH NOTES
On Windows, arguments with wildcards are expanded, ignoring case and
leaving out hidden and system files.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zip (1),
.BR unzip (1)
